<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gwadar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gwadar is a port city on the Makran coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balochistan">Balochistan</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, on a hammerhead peninsula facing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-sea">Arabian Sea</a>. Granted by the Khan of Kalat to an Omani prince in the 1780s, it remained an Omani possession until it was sold to Pakistan in 1958. Since the 2000s a deep-water port has been developed there with Chinese investment.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gwadar.jpg" alt="Gwadar" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shayhaq Baloch · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gwadar_city,_the_doors_of_Air.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
